distinguishes a fold that WROTE a SNAPSHOT from a nothing-to-fold / no-safe-gap / below-threshold pass (e.g. a distinct non-error return code from _compact_locked, or detecting a newly-created -SNAPSHOT.json), since all of those currently return 0 and the driver counts every rc==0 as compacted.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'As a second guard the driver counts a ticket as compacted only when the fold actually wrote a SNAPSHOT, so a nothing-to-fold pass is reported honestly rather than as work done.'","compact_txn.py:368-370 returns 0 on 'nothing to fold'; line 386 returns 0 on 'no safe horizon gap'; line 352-354 returns 0 on the in-lock threshold re-check; the success path also returns 0","compact.py:255 — driver treats rc==0 as compacted (`if rc == 0: compacted += 1`)","AC2 requires 'if selected is not counted as compacted' but the return contract cannot distinguish folded-a-snapshot from nothing-to-fold"],"finding":"The plan's 'second guard' (count a ticket as compacted only when the fold actually wrote a SNAPSHOT) has no achievable mechanism under the current return contract: _compact_locked returns 0 both on a successful fold and on the nothing-to-fold / no-safe-gap / below-threshold branches, and the driver counts every rc==0 as compacted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa6cdb122315cd902","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, part 1 ('As a second guard the driver counts a ticket as compacted only when the fold actually wrote a SNAPSHOT'); AC line 2","norm_id":"ne29c25e676a7e372","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A ticket over the raw threshold whose foldable count is zero (or whose horizon gap is unsafe) is folded, writes no SNAPSHOT, yet returns 0 and is tallied as compacted — the lying-count the plan set out to prevent","AC2's 'second sweep reports zero compacted' assertion fails because nothing-to-fold passes still count"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Give _compact_locked/compact_cli a distinct success-with-snapshot signal (e.g. a dedicated exit code or an out-param) and have compact_all_cli increment `compacted` only on that signal; keep rc==0-no-snapshot as a skipped/'nothing to fold' outcome.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The Testing section lists a 'Failure path' (rejected push leaves clone commits intact and reports failure) but there is no corresponding Acceptance Criterion, so this described deliverable has no covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda96b6e298861373","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing 'Failure path' vs Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nebb82e6b1438a918","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add AC: '[ ] A sweep whose push is rejected reports the failure and leaves the clone's commits intact — a test asserts non-corrupting behavior and a failure exit/summary.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify failure observability for compact-sweep.yml (e.g. a failure-notification step and/or a CloudWatch/heartbeat signal, matching reconcile-bridge.yml:273-392) so a silently-failing sweep does not re-introduce unbounded log growth undetected.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The new workflow copies its store-mount and identity steps verbatim in shape.' — scopes the copy to store-mount + identity, not the reconciler's Notify-on-failure / CloudWatch steps","reconcile-bridge.yml:273-288 has a 'Notify on bridge failure' step and :367-392 publishes run failure/success to CloudWatch","Absence: no acceptance criterion or Testing bullet covers detecting a failed/stalled sweep run"],"finding":"The new scheduled sweep workflow specifies no failure observability/alerting; the plan copies only the reconciler's 'store-mount and identity steps verbatim in shape' and omits the reconciler's failure-notification and CloudWatch steps, so a silently-failing 6-hourly sweep would let event logs grow unbounded again with no signal — the very regression this ticket exists to prevent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff26f930c3b176078","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach §2 'Trigger it out of band'; Scope: .github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml","norm_id":"neccd16b9eb36f6f3","priority":0.5,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A sweep run fails its push or errors mid-fold on every 6-hour cycle and nobody notices because nothing alerts","The workflow is accidentally disabled and log growth silently resumes"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that the new workflow also copies the reconciler's 'Notify on bridge failure' step (and, on the canonical repo, a run-failure CloudWatch metric or equivalent heartbeat) so a stalled/failing sweep raises an alert.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify a timeout-minutes budget and a concurrency group (cancel-in-progress: false) for compact-sweep.yml, mirroring reconcile-bridge.yml:54-56 and :80, so a long/hung sweep is bounded and dispatched+scheduled runs do not overlap.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Context: compaction 'held the ONE store write lock for up to 13m53s'","reconcile-bridge.yml:80 sets `timeout-minutes: 60` and :54-56 declares a `concurrency` group with `cancel-in-progress: false`","Absence: neither the workflow Scope bullet nor Acceptance Criteria mention timeout-minutes or a concurrency group"],"finding":"The plan does not name a timeout-minutes budget or a concurrency group for the sweep workflow. The original close-path fold held a write lock for up to 13m53s, so a full sweep folding many tickets can run long; without an explicit timeout a hung run consumes billed runner minutes indefinitely, and without a concurrency guard two scheduled/dispatched runs can overlap.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc448afd322ebdec5","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach §2; Scope: .github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml","norm_id":"n606787d0c5019b5b","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A large backfill sweep runs unexpectedly long and burns hosted-runner minutes","A workflow_dispatch fires while a scheduled run is mid-sweep, producing two overlapping folders"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","n